NAME
       printenv - print environment variables

SYNOPSIS
       printenv [NAME...]

DESCRIPTION
       Without arguments, printenv prints every environment variable as
       NAME=VALUE, one per line. With names, it prints only their values.
       It exits with 1 when a named variable is not set.

       Only exported variables are in the environment; a variable set in the
       shell without export is not shown. "echo $NAME" shows either kind.

EXAMPLES
           printenv PATH
           printenv | grep -i lang

SEE ALSO
       env(1), bash(1), export(1)
